UNAPPLIED SOURCE REPAIR FOR beads_rust #508

Recorded against main e6faabc73de1af6ce657c285407eb0c63e5c5582.
Expected input blobs:
  src/storage/sqlite.rs  b81de67662561de867288bcf3dc92505517bfb67
  src/config/mod.rs      b51514a7b44aa7f63edd4e37425cf2f28ef60c3a

This file does not alter the compiled Rust source. No runtime pass is claimed.
Apply and compile in a complete checkout before publishing an active repair.

There are two distinct failure mechanisms:
* The positive pre-install fixture supplies malformed bytes as a real engine
  certificate; preserve healthy engine-created metadata there. Keep the
  separate malformed-certificate refusal controls unchanged.
* On an incomplete/invalid checkpoint result, consumed SqliteStorage runs a
  new real TRUNCATE in Drop because prior mutations remain counted. Disable
  only this implicit checkpoint for the consumed live compaction handle,
  before the explicit checkpoint. Do not falsify mutation accounting, skip
  the explicit checkpoint, broaden certificate quarantine, or weaken witnesses.

The patch adds a handle-local teardown policy, keeps ordinary opens on their
existing policy, and leaves the installed/reopened handle and private source
on their normal paths. Explicit checkpoint admission, completion validation,
TRUNCATE-to-PASSIVE fallback, lease cleanup, installation and rollback remain.

Validation here: reviewed source hunks, checked patch syntax and whitespace.
Not performed: full-file patch application, Rust compilation, rustfmt, Clippy,
Rust tests, or release qualification. Verify all struct initializers compile.

Suggested application in a clean, complete checkout:
